  <note>
    <title>Chapel Street Walk — The Brick and Timber House</title>
    <content><![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd">
<en-note>
<div>16 August 1595, evening at Henley Street.</div>
<div>Walked down Chapel Street in Stratford this afternoon with Anne and my brother Richard, looking across at the corner house by the Guild Chapel. Brick and timber, three storeys high, a broken pane upstairs, and nettles standing at the gate. Richard tapped the wall with his stick and judged the framing sound under the neglect. Anne stood longer looking past the gate into the ground behind it and said she knew what she would do with the garden.</div>
<div>I asked no one in the street whose the house is, nor what it would cost. Walking back toward Henley Street I asked Anne for three years. She answered that she will give me till she believes me.</div>
</en-note>]]></content>
    <created>20250816T183000Z</created>
    <updated>20250816T183000Z</updated>
    <tag>stratford</tag>
    <tag>chapel-street</tag>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Mechanicals Casting — Notes After the Jackdaw</title>
    <content><![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd">
<en-note>
<div>22 November 1595, late at Great St Helen's after the Jackdaw.</div>
<div>Read the three casting sheets to Will Kemp across the table. He stood up from the bench and roared Ercles' vein so loud Agnes dropped a jug. Then he sat down again, read the three leaves through a second time, and said, "Thou'st put me in, thou villain." When I told him aloud about the ass's head — which is still spoken, not yet on paper — he laughed till he spilled his ale and Agnes charged us double.</div>
<div>Working points before writing the rehearsal scene: the three sheets stop cleanly after the casting; keep the other five tradesmen plain, earnest, and dead serious about their parts so Bottom's ambition carries against honest gravity rather than cheap mockery.</div>
</en-note>]]></content>
    <created>20251122T211000Z</created>
    <updated>20251122T211000Z</updated>
    <tag>writing</tag>
    <tag>mechanicals</tag>
  </note>
